<task id="t00872">
	<title>Main fuse (multi-fuse)</title>
	<taskbody>
		<context id="e05133">
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e05134">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e05135">
									<image align="center" placement="break" scale="95" href="images/N_SP327_D12_040_1.jpg"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<p>If the main fuse (multi-fuse) is blown, follow these steps to remove it:</p>
		</context>
		<steps id="e05136">
			<step>
				<cmd>Make sure the vehicle is in the <term translate="no">OFF</term> position.</cmd>
			</step>
			<step>
				<cmd>Disconnect the negative 12V battery cable.</cmd>
			</step>
			<step>
				<cmd>Remove the nuts as shown.</cmd>
			</step>
			<step>
				<cmd>Replace the fuse with a new one of the same rating.</cmd>
			</step>
			<step>
				<cmd>Reinstall in the reverse order of removal.</cmd>
			</step>
		</steps>
		<postreq id="e05137">
			<note type="note" id="e05138">
				<p>Visually inspect the 12V battery cap to make sure it is closed securely. If the 12V battery cap is not securely latched, influx of moisture into the electrical system may damage the system.</p>
			</note>
		</postreq>
	</taskbody>
	<related-links>
